11. Safety architecture

Because the consumer is breastfeeding and therefore infant exposure can matter, I’d set a higher internal standard than “legally sellable supplement.”

Before launch:

OB/GYN + IBCLC + registered dietitian + supplement regulatory counsel + qualified formulation scientist review.

Then require the contract manufacturer to operate under applicable dietary-supplement cGMP requirements and establish identity/purity/strength/composition specifications and contaminant testing appropriate to the ingredients.

I’d want third-party finished-product testing rather than relying solely on supplier certificates.

And the website should explicitly route persistent low supply, infant weight concerns, dehydration concerns, pain, latch problems, etc. toward appropriate medical/lactation evaluation rather than presenting Momma Milk as treatment.

